# A variable that nobody wrote a type for begins as a Float64Array, so use alone says that it holds one, and rows out of a parse are stored into it later: a list of numbers.
# The front of the loop asked for the view alone, and the list ran the closed copy, twenty-two times as slow. The other of the two is a member of the front.
# RUN: walk f2:Body mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f2:Body
# CHECK: = TypeTest {{*}}testedType=Float64Array
# CHECK: = TypeTest {{*}}testedType=Array<number>
